    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ac4cfbf1"
      },
      "source": [
        "Gemma is a family of lightweight, state-of-the-art open models built from the same research and technology used to create the [Gemini](https://deepmind.google/technologies/gemini/#introduction) models. Gemma 4 is designed to be the world's most efficient open-weight model family."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fecd5621"
      },
      "source": [
        "This document provides a guide to performing basic text inference with Gemma 4 using the Hugging Face `transformers` library. It covers environment setup, model loading, and various text generation scenarios including single-turn prompts, structured multi-turn conversations, and applying system instructions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "27e0cf0a"
      },
      "source": [
        "This notebook will run on T4 GPU."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "72effefe"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Install Python packages\n",
        "\n",
        "Install the Hugging Face libraries required for running the Gemma model and making requests."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "65bafd3f"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Install PyTorch & other libraries\n",
        "!pip install torch accelerate\n",
        "\n",
        "# Install the transformers library\n",
        "!pip install \"transformers>=5.10.1\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0deb7697"
      },
      "source": [
        "[Dialog](https://github.com/google-deepmind/dialog) is a library to manipulate and display conversations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f71c4a36"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip install dialog"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5e5b5400"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Load Model\n",
        "\n",
        "Use `transformers` library to load the pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6925e51d"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
              "model_id": "0fa207fdb5a04696bc80800331aa90eb",
              "version_major": 2,
              "version_minor": 0
            },
            "text/plain": [
              "Loading weights:   0%|          | 0/1951 [00:00<?, ?it/s]"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "MODEL_ID = \"google/gemma-4-E2B-it\" # @param [\"google/gemma-4-E2B-it\", \"google/gemma-4-E4B-it\", \"google/gemma-4-12B-it\", \"google/gemma-4-31B-it\", \"google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "from transformers import pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "txt_pipe = pipeline(\n",
        "    task=\"text-generation\",\n",
        "    model=MODEL_ID,\n",
        "    device_map=\"auto\",\n",
        "    dtype=\"auto\"\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "14a77834"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Run text generation\n",
        "\n",
        "Once you have the Gemma model loaded and configured in a `pipeline` object, you can send prompts to the model. The following example code shows a basic request using the `text_inputs` parameter:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 8,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f9a6a5d9"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stderr",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "[transformers] Both `max_new_tokens` (=256) and `max_length`(=20) seem to have been set. `max_new_tokens` will take precedence. Please refer to the documentation for more information. (https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/main_classes/text_generation)\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "<|turn>user\n",
            "Roses are..<turn|>\n",
            "<|turn>model\n",
            "Here are a few ways to complete the phrase \"Roses are...\":\n",
            "\n",
            "**Focusing on the color:**\n",
            "\n",
            "* **Roses are red.** (A classic, though slightly contradictory!)\n",
            "* **Roses are beautiful.**\n",
            "* **Roses are pink.**\n",
            "\n",
            "**Focusing on the feeling/meaning:**\n",
            "\n",
            "* **Roses are lovely.**\n",
            "* **Roses are sweet.**\n",
            "* **Roses are a sign of affection.**\n",
            "\n",
            "**A slightly more poetic answer:**\n",
            "\n",
            "* **Roses are a memory.**\n",
            "\n",
            "**Which one feels right to you? 😊**\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "output = txt_pipe(text_inputs=\"<|turn>user\\nRoses are..<turn|>\\n<|turn>model\\n\")\n",
        "print(output[0]['generated_text'].removesuffix(\"<turn|>\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4a6b0e86"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Use Dialog library"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 9,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "11ba5931"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "<|turn>user\n",
            "Roses are...<turn|>\n",
            "<|turn>model\n",
            "Here are a few ways to complete the phrase \"Roses are...\":\n",
            "\n",
            "**Focusing on the scent:**\n",
            "\n",
            "* **...fragrant.**\n",
            "* **...scented.**\n",
            "\n",
            "**Focusing on the visual:**\n",
            "\n",
            "* **...beautiful.**\n",
            "* **...vibrant.**\n",
            "* **...red.**\n",
            "\n",
            "**Focusing on the emotion (the most classic completion):**\n",
            "\n",
            "* **...a symbol of love.**\n",
            "* **...a declaration.**\n",
            "* **...perfect.**\n",
            "\n",
            "**If you want a simple, classic answer, I recommend:**\n",
            "\n",
            "**\"Roses are beautiful.\"** or **\"Roses are a symbol of love.\"**\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
              "model_id": "f5fe85a051db45298fe85ed09f989df5",
              "version_major": 2,
              "version_minor": 0
            },
            "text/plain": [
              "<dialog._src.widget.Conversation object at 0x7957faa35ac0>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {
            "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
              "colab": {
                "custom_widget_manager": {
                  "url": "https://ssl.gstatic.com/colaboratory-static/widgets/colab-cdn-widget-manager/2b70e893a8ba7c0f/manager.min.js"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import dialog\n",
        "from transformers import GenerationConfig\n",
        "config = GenerationConfig.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID)\n",
        "config.max_new_tokens = 512\n",
        "\n",
        "conv = dialog.Conversation(\n",
        "    dialog.User(\"Roses are...\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "output = txt_pipe(text_inputs=conv.as_text(), return_full_text=False, generation_config=config)\n",
        "conv += dialog.Model(output[0]['generated_text'].removesuffix(\"<turn|>\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(conv.as_text())\n",
        "conv.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "56b2e017"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Use a prompt template\n",
        "\n",
        "When generating content with more complex prompting, use a prompt template to structure your request. A prompt template allows you to specify input from specific roles, such as `user` or `model`, and is a required format for managing multi-turn chat interactions with Gemma models. The following example code shows how to construct a prompt template for Gemma:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6a2d979f"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Beneath the waves, where sunlight dies,\n",
            "A shadow stirs, with ancient sighs.\n",
            "The Kraken wakes, a monstrous might,\n",
            "With tentacles of endless night.\n",
            "\n",
            "A crushing grip, a salty dread,\n",
            "Where ships are lost and hope is dead.\n",
            "A legend spun of ink and brine,\n",
            "A primal fear, a dark design.\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from transformers import GenerationConfig\n",
        "config = GenerationConfig.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID)\n",
        "config.max_new_tokens = 512\n",
        "\n",
        "messages = [\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"role\": \"user\",\n",
        "        \"content\": [\n",
        "            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Write a short poem about the Kraken.\"},\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    }\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "output = txt_pipe(messages, return_full_text=False, generation_config=config)\n",
        "print(output[0]['generated_text'].removesuffix(\"<turn|>\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f07df76c"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Multi-turn conversation\n",
        "\n",
        "In a multi-turn setup, the conversation history is preserved as a sequence of alternating `user` and `model` roles. This cumulative list serves as the model's memory, ensuring that each new output is informed by the preceding dialogue.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cccece0d"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stderr",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "[transformers] You seem to be using the pipelines sequentially on GPU. In order to maximize efficiency please use a dataset\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "<|turn>user\n",
            "Write a short poem about the Kraken.<turn|>\n",
            "<|turn>model\n",
            "In depths where sunlight cease,\n",
            "A shadow vast and deep,\n",
            "The Kraken wakes with might,\n",
            "A terror to the sleep.\n",
            "With tentacles of ink,\n",
            "It pulls the ocean's brink.<turn|>\n",
            "<|turn>user\n",
            "Now with the Siren.<turn|>\n",
            "<|turn>model\n",
            "Where coral sleeps in silent grace,\n",
            "A melody floats from the sea,\n",
            "The Siren calls with silver thread,\n",
            "A siren song for all to see.\n",
            "With eyes of emerald, deep and wide,\n",
            "She lures the sailor to the tide.\n",
            "A siren's kiss, a deadly art,\n",
            "That breaks the sailor's guarded heart.\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
              "model_id": "3dc0a328537a4d699668f37e75f43d7a",
              "version_major": 2,
              "version_minor": 0
            },
            "text/plain": [
              "<dialog._src.widget.Conversation object at 0x7955701cc0e0>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {
            "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
              "colab": {
                "custom_widget_manager": {
                  "url": "https://ssl.gstatic.com/colaboratory-static/widgets/colab-cdn-widget-manager/2b70e893a8ba7c0f/manager.min.js"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import dialog\n",
        "from transformers import GenerationConfig\n",
        "config = GenerationConfig.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID)\n",
        "config.max_new_tokens = 512\n",
        "\n",
        "# User turn #1\n",
        "conv = dialog.Conversation(\n",
        "    dialog.User(\"Write a short poem about the Kraken.\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Model response #1\n",
        "output = txt_pipe(text_inputs=conv.as_text(), return_full_text=False, generation_config=config)\n",
        "conv += dialog.Model(output[0]['generated_text'].removesuffix(\"<turn|>\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "# User turn #2\n",
        "conv += dialog.User(\"Now with the Siren.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Model response #2\n",
        "output = txt_pipe(text_inputs=conv.as_text(), return_full_text=False, generation_config=config)\n",
        "conv += dialog.Model(output[0]['generated_text'].removesuffix(\"<turn|>\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(conv.as_text())\n",
        "conv.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
